  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 314 AM CDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nThere is a 15-20% chance for rain on Wednesday afternoon which \nmay bring clouds to the area. If this occurs and cloud cover is \nwidespread, this would eliminate the need for the Heat Advisory\nto be extended in time. Any storm that does form may be pulse-\nlike and occur in the afternoon and diminish near sunset.\n\nRain chances keep diminishing and are getting pushed further \nout in time. There were a few models showing rain towards the \nend of this week, but now the weather looks mostly dry. Though, \nthe signal for more widespread rain to occur Saturday into \nSunday (30-50%) has been pretty consistent as that ridge begins \nto hopefully push east. If the ridge stays put, it'll be more \ndifficult to get rain any further south than central MO. \n\nHighs will be in the 90s to end the week with temperatures \nlowering into the 80s for next weekend. Now, there is some hope\non the horizon with high temperatures threatening to drop into\nthe 70s for the start of next week. However, the spread in\ntemperatures for that far out is pretty large due to the\nuncertainty in the strength of the cold air advection associated\nwith the front. The average high temperature across the area\ncould be in the upper 70s with a range of about 10 degrees with\nthe warmer end being in the lower 80s and the cooler end being\nin the lower 70s. We'll continue to monitor the front incoming\nearly next week to see if cooler temperatures are actually on\ntheir way or if the models are giving us false hope.",
